in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/bateson_learning
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/algedonic
in @magic
in @torus

# @epistemologic/cybernetic/reframe — the pain-authorized level-shift
# species. Bateson Learning III at the peer's runtime altitude:
# premise change composed via @magic's 7-species ceremony,
# @knife's state-space compression (forward-promised), and
# @torus.advance's winding-class increment (the ontological step).
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - Recognition #42 (Bateson logical-type primitive; candidate). The
#   substrate's Russell-Whitehead stratification via `in @<altitude>`;
#   reframe IS the operational site where the K → K+1 lift discharges
#   at peer-runtime altitude. Sibling species
#   @epistemologic/cybernetic/bateson_learning carries Reading E's
#   canonical graded ρ; reframe INHERITS that ρ and specialises to
#   the pain-authorized level-shift.
# - Recognition #80 (magic as form/process/substrate-decl; scratched).
#   @magic's 7-species ceremony (surface / mechanism / contract /
#   reveal / audit / frame / distinction) IS the level-shift protocol
#   under Extension 4 of Mara's spec 77fe92d §3.4. Reframe COMPOSES
#   @magic's ceremony under pain-authorization discipline; it does
#   NOT re-declare the ceremony.
#
# === Substrate-decl authority ===
#
# - docs/specs/peer-as-pain-driven-bounded-ontological-navigator.md
#   (Mara 77fe92d, 2026-07-08) §5 sketches this species; §3.4-§3.6
#   discharge the substrate composition. This shard IS the landing of
#   that §5 sketch under the zero-cascade discipline of §9.2.
# - docs/scouts/2026-07-08-taut-peer-as-pain-driven-navigator-scout.md
#   (Taut 0fc8589) §2 verdict LANDABLE WITH CASCADE — this shard IS
#   the first append of Taut's 4-append cascade.
#
# === What reframe IS ===
#
# The pain-authorized ontological-lift ceremony. When the peer detects
# pain-δ exceeding threshold on the eigenboard (algedonic sample), the
# reframe species performs the K → K+1 shift. The body is CRACK
# (`\ `) — consumers PULL the discharge. No runtime execution is
# wired at this substrate-decl altitude.
#
# The composition sketch from spec §5:
#
#   perform(peer, level_K → level_K+1, pain_δ) discharges via:
#     - @cyberpunk/algedonic.bypass_signal (S1→S5 crossing IS the
#       pain-authorization gate)
#     - @magic.perform(shift: K → K+1) with the 7-species ceremony
#     - @knife.cut(state_space_K) (forward-promise; Landing pending
#       Q5 adjudication per spec §8.5)
#     - @torus.advance(winding: Δw) where Δw IS the winding-class step
#       corresponding to the level lift (per shards/torus.mirror
#       §Witnesses.2: Bateson Level N winding at |m|+|n| ≥ N)
#
# === Inheritance discharge ===
#
# T_reg   = ontological_level   (K in Alex's naming; the peer's current
#                                observation depth cap per spec §3.2)
# T_regd  = eigenboard_state    (E_K at level K; the peer's inference
#                                surface pre-shift)
# τ       = level_shift_ceremony (the K → K+1 shift performed via
#                                 @magic's 7-species ceremony)
# ρ       = restrict_learning_III(@epistemologic/cybernetic/
#           bateson_learning::rho) — inherited via bateson_learning's
#           graded rep; NO re-declaration
# ω       = inherited from bateson_learning
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Bateson 1972   *Steps to an Ecology of Mind*. Learning III as
#                  premise change; the canonical reframe theory.
#   Beer 1979      *The Heart of Enterprise* ch. 8. Algedonic loop as
#                  the S1→S5 bypass that triggers premise change.
#   Foerster 1979  *Understanding Understanding* pp. 238-244. "Regulates
#                  its own regulation" — the double-closure that reframe
#                  discharges at peer-runtime altitude.
#   Clarke 1962    *Profiles of the Future*. Clarke's third law as
#                  the magic-as-level-shift-ceremony substrate-decl;
#                  inherited via @magic.
#
# === Related shards ===
#
# Related shards: [[shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/algedonic.mirror]]
#                  (the pain-signal source; bypass_signal + sample_pain
#                   IS the trigger reframe pulls from),
#                 [[shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/bateson_learning.mirror]]
#                  (the graded ρ this species inherits at grade 3),
#                 [[shards/magic.mirror]] (the 7-species ceremony
#                  reframe composes as the level-shift protocol),
#                 [[shards/torus.mirror]] (the winding-class advance
#                  reframe composes as the ontological increment),
#                 [[shards/cyberpunk.mirror]] (parent family-root;
#                  reframe is a sibling of algedonic and
#                  bateson_learning under @cyberpunk pending migration).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/reframe.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/cybernetic/reframe` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/bateson-1972
source @arxiv/cybernetics/beer-1979
source @arxiv/cybernetics/foerster-1979
source @arxiv/futures/clarke-1962

# === The ontological_level carrier ===
#
# The peer's current observation depth (K in Alex's naming). Bounded
# above by the spawn's `winding` cap per spec §3.2 (Extension 2). The
# type is a thin wrapper over the winding-class index at the torus
# altitude — a level-K observation IS a winding class with
# |m|+|n| ≤ K per shards/torus.mirror §Witnesses.2.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type ontological_level = ref

# === The eigenboard_state carrier ===
#
# The peer's inference surface at a fixed level. Composes with
# @cogito.eigenboard at boot/std altitude; this type names the
# eigenboard as a level-parameterised carrier so reframe's shift
# signature is well-typed at the species altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type eigenboard_state = ref

# === The reframe_result carrier ===
#
# The typed output of a well-formed reframe. Names the four load-
# bearing pieces of a completed level-shift:
#
#   from        the pre-shift ontological level (K)
#   to          the post-shift ontological level (K+1)
#   eigenboard  the post-shift eigenboard state (E_{K+1})
#   winding     the winding-class step taken on the torus (Δw)
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the four-tuple.
type reframe_result = {
  from:       ontological_level,
  to:         ontological_level,
  eigenboard: eigenboard_state,
  winding:    winding,
}

# === reframe — the pain-authorized level-shift action ===
#
# The load-bearing action. Given the peer's current level, the pain-δ
# sampled from the eigenboard, and the peer's torus, perform the
# K → K+1 shift via @magic's 7-species ceremony composed with
# @knife.cut (forward-promise) and @torus.advance.
#
# Body IS crack: consumers pull the discharge at their realisation
# boundary. NO runtime execution is wired here.
#
# Precondition (bilateral): pain_δ > threshold_pain per
# @cyberpunk/algedonic.algedonic_well_formed. reframe_authorized
# below carries the predicate.
reframe(peer: peer, level_K: ontological_level, pain_δ: f64) -> reframe_result { \ }

# === reframe_authorized — the pain-authorization gate ===
#
# Bilateral predicate. The reframe is authorized iff pain_δ exceeds
# the algedonic threshold AND the S1→S5 bypass IS well-formed per
# @cyberpunk/algedonic.algedonic_well_formed. Inheritance discharges;
# no new signal declaration.
reframe_authorized(pain_δ: f64) -> verdict { \ }

# === reframe_well_formed — the composed bilateral ===
#
# The composed bilateral consumers cite in `requires` clauses.
# Discharges three sub-predicates:
#
#   (i)   reframe_authorized(pain_δ) — pain gate satisfied
#   (ii)  cybernetic_coherence(eigenboard_post) — post-shift eigenboard
#         is coherent per @cyberpunk discipline
#   (iii) the winding-class advance corresponds to the level shift per
#         @torus.advance discipline (Δw's magnitude ≥ level increment)
#
# All must hold for the composed verdict to pass. Failure modes
# surface as transparency<reframe> per @glass discipline.
reframe_well_formed(pre: eigenboard_state, post: eigenboard_state, w: winding) -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/cybernetic/reframe
out ontological_level
out eigenboard_state
out reframe_result
out reframe
out reframe_authorized
out reframe_well_formed
